%index
GetConsoleCP
Retrieves the input code page used by the console associated with the calling process.
%group
Win32 kernel32
%prm

%inst
Retrieves the input code page used by the console associated with the
calling process.

[戻り値]
This function has no parameters.
The return value is a code that identifies the code page. For a list
of identifiers, see [Code Page
Identifiers](/windows/win32/intl/code-page-identifiers). If the
return value is zero, the function has failed. To get extended error
information, call
[**GetLastError**](/windows/win32/api/errhandlingapi/nf-errhandlingapi-getlasterror).

[備考]
A code page maps 256 character codes to individual characters.
Different code pages include different special characters, typically
customized for a language or a group of languages. To retrieve more
information about a code page, including it's name, see the
[**GetCPInfoEx**](/windows/win32/api/winnls/nf-winnls-getcpinfoexa)
function. To set a console's input code page, use the
[**SetConsoleCP**](setconsolecp.md) function. To set and query a
console's output code page, use the
[**SetConsoleOutputCP**](setconsoleoutputcp.md) and
[**GetConsoleOutputCP**](getconsoleoutputcp.md) functions.


