[備考]
The format of the returned keys and values is one or more
null-terminated strings, followed by a final null character. Each
string has the following form: key=string The GetProfileSection
function is not case-sensitive; the strings can be a combination of
uppercase and lowercase letters. This operation is atomic; no updates
to the Win.ini file are allowed while the keys and values for the
section are being copied to the buffer. Windows Server 2003 and
Windows XP/2000: Calls to profile functions may be mapped to the
registry instead of to the initialization files. This mapping occurs
when the initialization file and section are specified in the
registry under the following key:
