Win32 kernel32
%prm
lpString1, lpString2
lpString1 : [wstr] Type: LPTSTR The first null-terminated string. This buffer must be large enough to contain both strings.
lpString2 : [wstr] Type: LPTSTR The null-terminated string to be appended to the string specified in the lpString1 parameter.
%inst
Appends one string to another.Warning Do not use. (Unicode)

[戻り値]
Type: LPTSTR If the function succeeds, the return value is a pointer
to the buffer. If the function fails, the return value is NULL and
lpString1 may not be null-terminated.

[備考]
> [!NOTE] > The winbase.h header defines lstrcat as an alias which
